Riseonly patch on zed 6b2aa1c (Apache-2.0 crates gpui, gpui_windows), applied by scripts/vendor-gpui.py after 0007.
A D3D11VA picture reaches the DirectX 11 renderer without a CPU copy (P149, P27 win step 2): on Windows
OwnedSurfaceFrame::shared_nv12 carries a SharedSurfaceHandle (an NT handle of an NV12 texture the decoder's
device shares with D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_SHARED_NTHANDLE and a keyed mutex) and keeps the producer's texture
alive with the frame. The renderer opens the handle once per shared texture with
ID3D11Device1::OpenSharedResource1, views its planes as R8 (t2) and R8G8 (t3), and draws it with the NV12
surface shader inside AcquireSync(0)/ReleaseSync(0). Other platforms are unchanged.

